No NETGEAR software in this project
-----------------------------------
No NETGEAR software is part of this project or of the images it builds. The
front-panel support (display, disk lights, Backup button) was written from
scratch, for interoperability, after studying how the hardware is wired.
Never commit or distribute NETGEAR files: the flash backup made during the
installation (image/readynas-flash.img), RAIDiator's system archives (*.tlz)
or its kernel modules (*.ko). .gitignore refuses them.


Third-party software in the system image
----------------------------------------
The image built by image/build.sh is a Debian 13 system (Linux, Samba,
rsync, mdadm, vsftpd, NUT, rclone, OpenSSH...). Those packages keep their own
licenses (many GPL), listed in /usr/share/doc/*/copyright inside the image.
Their source code is available from Debian for the exact versions installed:
https://www.debian.org/distrib/packages and https://snapshot.debian.org
(the list of versions: dpkg-query -W inside the image). When you distribute
an image, offer that source along with it, as the GPL requires.

The web interface is built with Svelte and Vite (MIT licenses).


